{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/189952-my-thoughts-one-mages-of-ethers","id":189952,"title":"My thoughts one Mages of Ethers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-06T23:12:52-07:00","id":189952,"title":"My thoughts one Mages of Ethers","content":"Hi watch DVD's MST3K, B movies of Science Fiction, since most of them are pulp it got me thinking, since these Science heroes and mages are mostly too Individual for Government and Corps they would run to forces that would supress there super science. A perfect example of this is the 1980's Cold Fusion debate.<br /> <br /> I the reason I posting this idea is that I working on my own idea about Science heroes that were supressed and made in the general world there ideas ridiculed and belittled, and in America most there tech was stolen and is used by corps as are modern tech,<br /> <br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T01:22:26-07:00","id":190018,"title":"","content":"Take a look at Nikola Tesla for one of the best real-world examples of such a thing in action. Look at the smear campaigns that Edison and others used against Tesla and alternating current versus Edisons devotion to direct current, including the electrocution of an elephant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T00:21:27-07:00","id":191178,"title":"","content":"Given the fact the most of the Writers of Pulps were Nerds expect Doc Savage he was a real mucho man, much like the creator of Mike Hammer. Now Doc Savage' was raised using Eugenics and gave Lobotomies to fix the criminals that he stopped.<br /> <br /> I want to use Doc Aeon as my version of Doc Savage in my sci fi idea, This world were a cabal of American government and corps supressed, smeared, and reverse engineering there tech to give the general mob water down versions of it.<br /> <br /> Hollow Earths and Warlord of Mars are places that this cabal has supressed from the general population,<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T02:02:44-08:00","id":1169856,"title":"","content":"Smear Campaigns are good idea,<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T15:04:50-08:00","id":1170291,"title":"","content":"Tesla is the classic example, but also look at Wilhelm Reich (his whole weird career is full of Etherite zaniness), Royal Rife (you can find &quot;Rife Machines&quot; for sale even now), Jose Delgado (Spanish researcher into mind control, aspiring Nephandi), and that Italian doctor currently trying to perform a head transplant without getting destroyed by Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T18:25:27-08:00","id":1170331,"title":"","content":"I think, from a style perspective, you tend to end up with<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Retro-Victorian Steam Punk</b>, which seams to be the prevailing style for the Tradition this past decade or so (GURPS Steampunk Tech and Castle Faulkenstein's Age of Steam sourcebook are good sources for visual and concept inspiration, as are the number of steampunk themed art books released in the past few years)</li> <li><b>Art Deco Pulp</b>, from the pulp fiction of the 1920s, 30s and 40s, which is probably still a favorite of Adventurer types (White Wolf's ADVENTURE! RPG is good reading, as are things like the Rocketeer, GURPS Cliffhangers, and Pulp Hero)</li> <li><b>Silver Age Science Fiction</b>, drawing on post-WW2 sci-fi comics and films up until around the mid to late 60s, probably a bigger influence on Ethernauts than any other group, as well as for Utopians looking for a nice lean and clean look for their ideal devices (see a lot of DC's Silver Age science fiction comics, including Adam Strange and others, as well as early Star Trek, sci-fi episodes of The Twilight Zone and the like.)</li> <li><b>New Age Science</b>, for those in love with the 80s and it's odd mix of bright optimism and internal anxieties (Buckaroo Banzai is the primary archetype, but also Back to the Future, Devo, and some other period sci-fi)</li> <li><b>Diesel Punk</b>, inspired by early German Expressionism films, WW1 and WW2 era engineering, and Film Noir (see some parts of Hellboy, Sandman Mystery Theater, Dark City, Sky Captain &amp; The World of Tomorrow, and the Crimson Skies game)</li> <li><b>ATOMICS!</b>, usually a variation on 2, 3 or 5, with a massive focus on atomic energy as the key to unlocking Ether, using it to empower everything from vehicles and ray guns to the human body and giant monsters</li> <li><b>Gothic Punk</b>, the ones that almost pass for &quot;normal&quot;, dressing like your average club crawler/young iconoclast with gear that looks like it was started in a science lab and finished in a garage workshop</li> </ol><br /> Science-wise, the modern ones probably are heavily into quantum mechanics, zero point energy, dark matter, non- Euclidean geometry, string theory, sixth dimensional constructs, SENS, and things of that nature, but I'm sure things like orgone, cold fusion, electrogravitics, and perpetual motion machines remain beloved aspects of the Tradition's history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}